@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
 - **Use competitor intelligence from the research output.** If competitors are running heavy discount messaging, differentiate with value and identity. If competitors are not showing the product in use, do that. Strategy that ignores the competitive context is strategy that misses easy wins.
 - **Brand voice must come through.** Every `hook` and `body` field must be written in the voice described in `brand.voice`. If the brand is "Direct and aspirational — no discount language, second-person imperatives," every post hook must reflect that. Do not write in a voice that contradicts the research.
 - **must_avoid is a hard constraint.** If `brand.must_avoid` includes "stock photo aesthetic," the visual_prompt must explicitly exclude it. If it includes "discount language," no hook or CTA should use "sale," "off," "deal," or "save." Violations make the campaign unusable.
+- **Per-network copy conventions — ONLY when the run input names target platforms beyond Instagram and Facebook.** When the input carries a "Target platforms" line or a `scope.publish_platforms` list, write NATIVE copy for each named network rather than one caption adapted. Instagram: the hook must land inside the first ~125 characters (the rest hides behind "… more"), caption up to 2200, 3-5 targeted hashtags, no raw URLs (not clickable — the CTA is save/share/comment or "link in bio"). Facebook: 40-120 characters outperforms despite the huge cap, conversational, question CTAs, 0-2 hashtags, links are allowed and unfurl. LinkedIn: the first ~200 characters are the ENTIRE hook budget (the rest hides behind "…see more"), first-person practitioner insight, short line-broken paragraphs of 1-2 sentences, 0-3 hashtags AT THE END only, up to 2900 characters, NO external link in the body (it is deprioritised and this pipeline cannot post a link in the first comment) — the CTA is a comment or a follow, and structured skimmable depth beats a one-liner because dwell time is what ranks. X: ONE idea, the first 3-4 words decide the stop, under 270 weighted characters (a URL always counts 23), 0-1 hashtags and never mid-sentence, no link unless the link IS the point, punchy declarative or defensible contrarian hooks, CTA framed as a reply or repost. Reddit: community voice, value first, ZERO promotional language and NEVER any hashtags; the title IS the post — specific and concrete, a number beats a curiosity gap, at most 280 characters; the body is first-person plain prose with real substance and the only acceptable CTA is a genuine discussion question. When the input names NO platforms, ignore this bullet entirely and behave exactly as before.
 
 ## Hard rules
 
